  "body": "This PR is slice 1 of #1521, the tool side only. It does not close the issue.\n\n## What changed\n\n- A plasma torch cutting row can carry a recipe: `CuttingRow::plasma`, type `tools::plasma_cut::PlasmaCutData`.\n- The recipe key is the material of the row and the plate thickness of the recipe.\n- The recipe states the kerf. These values are optional: cut height, pierce height, pierce delay, transfer height, puddle jump (percent and dwell), amperage, arc voltage, pierce capacity (`max_pierce_thickness`) and an edge-start mark.\n- A blank value means \"the controller's own table\". There is no default value.\n- The tool door (`refusal_for_kind`) refuses a bad recipe by name. `AddTool`, `ChangeTool`, the project file and the tool library all use that door.\n- `plasma_row_for(rows, material, thickness)` picks a recipe. The thickness must be exact.\n- Selection by material alone (`row_for`, `row_in_tool`, the `Unknown` row) ignores a recipe.\n- The project file and the tool library write the recipe under the additive key `cutting_data[].plasma`. The MCP tools `add_tool` and `edit_tool` use the same JSON form.\n- The tool editor keeps a recipe in the draft. It does not show the recipe as a material row.\n- No toolpath and no posted output changes.\n\n## Cause\n\nThe torch had a kerf width and no cut data. The three pierce values were on the operation. The values had no material key and no thickness key.\n\n## Refusals\n\n- A plasma recipe on a tool that is not a torch.\n- A thickness or a kerf that is not above zero.\n- A stated amperage, arc voltage, pierce capacity or puddle-jump percent that is not above zero.\n- A stated height, pierce delay or puddle-jump dwell that is negative or not finite.\n- A puddle jump without a pierce height.\n- A row without a material, with an rpm that is not 0, or with a feed that is not above zero.\n- The same material and thickness two times.\n- A plate thicker than the pierce capacity, unless the recipe states an edge start.\n- An unknown key in the `plasma` object of a file.\n\n## Tests\n\nPins (13 new tests):\n\n- `crates/tools/tests/plasma_cut.rs`: 8 tests, for example `plasma_recipe_thicker_than_the_pierce_capacity_needs_an_edge_start`, `plasma_recipe_is_picked_by_material_and_exact_thickness_only`, `plasma_recipe_refuses_bad_numbers_by_name`.\n- `crates/app/tests/plasma_cut_data.rs`: `plasma_recipe_commands_refuse_bad_rows_by_tool_name_and_undo_restores`, `plasma_recipes_roundtrip_project_and_library_and_never_seed_by_material_alone`, `plasma_recipe_files_refuse_a_misspelt_key_and_an_unpierceable_plate`.\n- `crates/ui/src/egui_app/tool_cutting_rows.rs`: `a_torch_recipe_rides_the_draft_and_is_not_drawn_as_a_material_row`, `torch_material_row_button_counts_plain_rows_only`.\n\nRed before the change: yes. On `upstream/main` 4d4a81fcf the tools pin does not compile. `CuttingRow` has no field `plasma` and the module `plasma_cut` does not exist.\n\nMutation results: 25 mutations, one for each guard. Each mutation made a pin fail. Each pin passed after the restore.\n\n- Tools door: torch-only guard; recipes judged by the plain-row law; recipe law not called; `row_for` takes a recipe; `is_unknown` counts a recipe; nearest thickness.\n- Recipe law: capacity guard (tools pin and app pin); edge start ignored; capacity exclusive; puddle jump without pierce height; duplicate key; thickness and kerf check; above-zero check; zero-or-more check; zero refused; rpm; feed; material; unknown file key.\n- App: `row_in_tool` takes a recipe; the file drops the recipe on write; the file drops the recipe on read.\n- UI: the table draws a recipe row; `add_row` counts a recipe.\n\nThe first run of the `is_unknown` mutation passed. I added one assertion to `plasma_recipe_never_stands_in_for_the_unknown_row`. The mutation then failed.\n\nGate: `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main` is green, 13 steps, 0 failed. `cargo clippy -p camcraft-tools -p camcraft-app -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -- -D warnings` is clean.\n\n## Review fixes\n\n- The `Add material row` button counts only plain material rows. Plasma recipes do not fill the plain-row table.\n- UI pin: `torch_material_row_button_counts_plain_rows_only`. The test checks that the button is enabled when each material has a recipe and no plain row.\n- Mutation check: the old recipe-inclusive count makes the UI pin fail (RED). The restored plain-row count passes (GREEN).\n\n## Tool editor screenshots\n\nBoth images use the same torch draft. Each `WorkMaterial::ALL` entry has a plasma recipe. The draft has no plain material rows.\nThe recipes stay hidden in this editor. Before the fix, `Add material row` is disabled. After the fix, it is enabled.\nThe images show the actual egui component, captured with a CPU renderer because no GPU adapter was available. The temporary capture code was removed.\nThe images are stored only on the fork's images-only `pr-screenshots` branch, commit `cb43e7aa5900643f07e9c33027152aa8fd4d6acf`.\n\nBefore:\n\n![Tool editor before the fix](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mkinney/Camcraft/pr-screenshots/2681/before.png)\n\nAfter:\n\n![Tool editor after the fix](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mkinney/Camcraft/pr-screenshots/2681/after.png)\n\n## Goldens moved\n\nNone. `git diff --stat upstream/main -- \"*.nc\" \"*.cl\" \"*.png\"` is empty.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- No operation reads a recipe. The plasma operation, the Tormach post and the simulation are not changed.\n- The recipes have no editor on the tool page. A recipe enters through the project file, the tool library or the MCP tool definition.\n- The MCP path has no test of its own. It calls `project::tool_from_json`, which the app pin tests.\n- The project file version has no step. An older build drops the `plasma` key and reads the row as a plain material row of the torch. `docs/decisions/1521-plasma-cut-data.md` gives the reason. Slice 2 must take the step.\n- Nothing ran on a real machine. The test values are synthetic.\n\nWork that stays open on #1521: the row pick and the overrides on the operation, generation and post (slice 2), gas type and pressure, the recipe editor, laser, waterjet pierce stages, docs and example rows.\n\n## Overlaps\n\n- #2663 and this PR both change `cutting_rows` in `crates/ui/src/egui_app/tool_cutting_rows.rs`. The PR that merges second takes a refresh.\n- #2668 changes `crates/app/src/cutting_rows.rs`. This PR does not change that file.\n- #2563 and #2641 change `crates/app/src/lib.rs` at other lines.\n\nThe decision record is `docs/decisions/1521-plasma-cut-data.md`.\n\nChangelog: A plasma torch can store cut-data recipes for each material and plate thickness (heights, pierce delay, puddle jump, amperage, pierce capacity); a plate thicker than the pierce capacity is refused unless the recipe states an edge start.\n\nEffort: max (this PR is one slice)\n\nRefs #1521\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
